- #48 - pyramid grid fallback order should depend on the piece's OWN
  desired position, not one global order. Currently (pieceGridSlots(),
  gnostica.ts) every piece that loses its preferred slot falls back to
  whichever slot is next in the single fixed PIECE_GRID_SLOTS order
  (N,S,E,W,U), regardless of which slot it actually wanted. Needs a
  per-orientation fallback priority list instead (e.g. N's own fallback
  order might not match S's) - exact per-position orders still TBD.
- #49 - require use/play moves to be meaningful, breaking from the literal
  rules text on purpose: a "use"/"play" that declines EVERY power step
  (0 steps actually taken) currently validates as a complete, submittable
  move - the "you can stop here" messaging around this is bad UI, since
  the player hasn't actually done anything. Spec, fully clarified:
    - Applies equally to use and play - a fully-declined play still isn't
      "meaningful" just because the card leaves hand (discarding it via
      the ALREADY-legal "discard <uid> draw 0" is the correct path for
      "I don't want this card's power," not play-then-decline).
    - Does NOT affect declining the TAIL of an already-started major
      arcana chain (>=1 step actually taken, rest declined) - that
      remains legal exactly as today (see the existing Lovers/etc. tests).
    - Fool (uid "00") is fully exempt - not a general "no supported
      power" carve-out, but because of the RULE that a drawn Fool card
      *must* be played, and it has no supported power at all (still
      pending the hidden-info-interaction precedent per Fool/World memory
      note) - so decline is its only possible outcome and must stay legal.
    - Wanting to do nothing at all (no card involved) stays via Pass /
      "discard draw 0", already fixed this session.
